us="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI CABLE INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAWADA, HISASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, MINORU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>GENJI TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IMAMURA KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAWADA HISASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA MINORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GENJI, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IMAMURA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAWADA, HISASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, MINORU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fiber amplifier uses an erbium-doped fiber core (1) in which a plurality of long-period fiber gratings (21) functioning as a gain equalizer are formed by an ultraviolet laser. Each of the fiber gratings (21) is irradiated with ultraviolet laser through the cladding layer of the optical fiber core (1) to provide periodic modulation for the refractive index of the fiber core. The fiber gratings (21) in the core (1) compensate for the wavelength dependency of gain to provide flat gain, resulting in uniform and efficient amplification over a wide range.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un amplificateur à fibres comportant une âme (1) de fibre dopée à l'erbium et plusieurs réseaux (21) de fibres de période longue fonctionnant comme égaliseurs de gain et commandés par un laser à UV. Chacun des réseaux de fibres (21) est irradié par le laser à UV à travers la couche d'enrobage de l'âme (1) de manière à produire une modulation périodique de l'indice de réfraction de l'âme (1). Le réseau (21) de fibres de l'âme (1) compense la dépendance du gain de la longueur d'onde, ce qui assure un gain linéaire et une amplification efficace sur une plage étendue.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>